SUMMARY:Deadline: A4 Residency Art Center: International Residency Fellowsh
 ip 2028 (Chengdu)
DESCRIPTION:The A4 Residency Art Center in Chengdu\, the residency platform
  of the A4 Art Museum in Luxelakes Eco-City\, opens its full-year 2028 rec
 ruitment.\n\nOrganisation: A4 Residency Art Center (A4 Art Museum)\nLocati
 on: Luxelakes Eco-City\, Tianfu New Area\, Chengdu\, China. Open worldwide
 .\nAward: Fully funded fellowship: private studio and accommodation\, roun
 d-trip economy airfare or second-class train ticket within a set budget\, 
 and a production grant of RMB 10\,000 per person/team for materials and pr
 oduction (excluding living expenses). No application fee.\nDuration: Appro
 ximately 8 weeks\, in the Spring 2028 (April to June) or Autumn 2028 (July
  to October) cycle.\n\nMore: https://www.a4artmuseum.com/en/a4-residencyar
 tcenter/residing/latest-recruitment/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk
 &utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.a4artmuseum.com/en/a4-residencyartcenter/residing/latest-re
 cruitment/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Luxelakes Eco-City\, Tianfu New Area\, Chengdu\, China. Open world
 wide.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:stimuleringsfonds-videotage-residency-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261104T163759Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261021
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261022
SUMMARY:Deadline: Stimuleringsfonds: Open Call Residency Videotage 2027 (Ho
 ng Kong)
DESCRIPTION:The Creative Industries Fund NL (Stimuleringsfonds) runs this r
 esidency with Videotage\, a Hong Kong-based non-profit media arts institut
 ion specialising in the promotion\, presentation\, creation and preservati
 on of moving image and media art in all forms and languages.\n\nOrganisati
 on: Stimuleringsfonds Creatieve Industrie (Creative Industries Fund NL) in
  collaboration with Videotage\, Hong Kong\nLocation: Residency takes place
  at Videotage in Hong Kong. Applicants must be established in the Netherla
 nds\, Aruba\, Bonaire\, Curacao\, Saba\, Sint Eustatius or Sint Maarten (K
 ingdom of the Netherlands) and registered in a business register within th
 e Kingdom of the Netherlands.\nAward: EUR 5\,000 for a two-month residency
  or EUR 6\,500 for a three-month residency\, paid by the Creative Industri
 es Fund NL to cover travel\, insurance\, living expenses\, compensation fo
 r time invested\, and material and transport costs. Accommodation\, use of
  the studio space and facilitation by Videotage are covered directly by th
 e Fund on top of this. No application fee.\nDuration: Two or three months 
 in 2027 (spring 2027)\; state your preferred period in the application.\n\
 nMore: https://www.stimuleringsfonds.nl/en/grants/open-call-videotage?utm_
 source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.stimuleringsfonds.nl/en/grants/open-call-videotage?utm_sour
 ce=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Residency takes place at Videotage in Hong Kong. Applicants must b
 e established in the Netherlands\, Aruba\, Bonaire\, Curacao\, Saba\, Sint
  Eustatius or Sint Maarten (Kingdom of the Netherlands) and registered in 
 a business register within the Kingdom of the Netherlands.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:stimuleringsfonds-jatiwangi-residency-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261104T163759Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261021
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261022
SUMMARY:Deadline: Stimuleringsfonds: Open Call Residency Jatiwangi art Fact
 ory 2027 (Indonesia)
DESCRIPTION:The Creative Industries Fund NL (Stimuleringsfonds) is recruiti
 ng one Netherlands-based designer\, architect or spatial practitioner for 
 a two-month residency in 2027 at Jatiwangi art Factory (JaF)\, an internat
 ionally recognised artistic collective based in a former roof tile factory
  in West Java\, Indonesia.\n\nOrganisation: Stimuleringsfonds Creatieve In
 dustrie (Creative Industries Fund NL) in collaboration with Jatiwangi art 
 Factory\, Indonesia\nLocation: Residency takes place at Jatiwangi art Fact
 ory in Jatiwangi\, West Java\, Indonesia. Applicants must be established i
 n the Netherlands\, Aruba\, Bonaire\, Curacao\, Saba\, Sint Eustatius or S
 int Maarten (Kingdom of the Netherlands) and registered in a business regi
 ster within the Kingdom of the Netherlands.\nAward: EUR 4\,500 subsidy for
  a two-month residency\, paid by the Creative Industries Fund NL. Accommod
 ation at Jatiwangi art Factory is provided: a small private container hous
 e furnished with two single beds and a bathroom/toilet. No application fee
 .\nDuration: Two months in 2027\n\nMore: https://www.stimuleringsfonds.nl/
 en/grants/open-call-residency-jatiwangi-art-factory?utm_source=artificialn
 ouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.stimuleringsfonds.nl/en/grants/open-call-residency-jatiwang
 i-art-factory?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Residency takes place at Jatiwangi art Factory in Jatiwangi\, West
  Java\, Indonesia. Applicants must be established in the Netherlands\, Aru
 ba\, Bonaire\, Curacao\, Saba\, Sint Eustatius or Sint Maarten (Kingdom of
  the Netherlands) and registered in a business register within the Kingdom
  of the Netherlands.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:sixi-air-residency-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261104T163759Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261115
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261116
SUMMARY:Deadline: Sixi Museum: SIXI AiR Open Call 2027 Spring & Autumn (Nan
 jing)
DESCRIPTION:The Sixi International Artist-in-Residence Project\, run by Six
 i Museum in Nanjing since 2024\, selects 4 artists across two three-month 
 sessions in 2027 (Spring\, March to May\, and Autumn\, September to Novemb
 er).\n\nOrganisation: Sixi Museum\nLocation: Nanjing\, China. Open to arti
 sts of all disciplines and cultural backgrounds\, aged 18 or older\, profi
 cient in Mandarin or English.\nAward: Round-trip flights\, visa applicatio
 n fees\, insurance\, and a private city-center apartment or loft studio on
  the outskirts\, plus a material allowance (amount not published)\, techni
 cal assistance\, airport pickup and translation support. NO artist fee or 
 stipend mentioned. No application fee.\nDuration: Three months: Spring 202
 7 (March to May) or Autumn 2027 (September to November).\n\nMore: https://
 siximuseum.com/en/residency/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_med
 ium=referral
URL:https://siximuseum.com/en/residency/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantd
 esk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Nanjing\, China. Open to artists of all disciplines and cultural b
 ackgrounds\, aged 18 or older\, proficient in Mandarin or English.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:acc-next-emerging-asian-artists-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261104T163759Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261025
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261026
SUMMARY:Deadline: 2027 ACC NEXT Emerging Asian Artists International Open C
 all (Gwangju)
DESCRIPTION:The National Asian Culture Center (ACC) in Gwangju seeks bold\,
  experimental work by emerging artists from Asia at the intersection of ar
 t and technology for its 2027 ACC NEXT exhibition. The theme is Prototype\
 ; works must not have been presented in another exhibition\, or must be re
 -created works.\n\nOrganisation: National Asian Culture Center (ACC)\nLoca
 tion: National Asian Culture Center\, Gwangju\, South Korea. Open to natio
 nals of Asian countries born on or after 1 January 1987\; artists born or 
 raised in Asia whose practice deeply engages with Asian identities may als
 o be considered regardless of nationality.\nAward: Artist fee of KRW 3\,00
 0\,000 per work\, an installation and materials budget of up to KRW 2\,000
 \,000 per work\, one round-trip international airfare (or domestic transpo
 rtation)\, and tentative accommodation at Asia Plex Studio. One artist or 
 team is additionally selected for the 2027 ACC CREATORS Residency through 
 an artist pitch review. For teams\, fees\, travel and accommodation go to 
 the team leader only.\nDuration: Exhibition of selected works at ACC in 20
 27\; selected artists must attend the installation\, opening and artist pi
 tch\n\nMore: https://www.acc.go.kr/en/board/board.do?PID=1001&boardID=NOTI
 CE&action=Read&idx=2866&utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=r
 eferral
URL:https://www.acc.go.kr/en/board/board.do?PID=1001&boardID=NOTICE&action=
 Read&idx=2866&utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:National Asian Culture Center\, Gwangju\, South Korea. Open to nat
 ionals of Asian countries born on or after 1 January 1987\; artists born o
 r raised in Asia whose practice deeply engages with Asian identities may a
 lso be considered regardless of nationality.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:matsu-biennial-4-open-call-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261104T163759Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261030
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261031
SUMMARY:Deadline: 4th Matsu Biennial International Open Call (Matsu Islands
 \, Taiwan)
DESCRIPTION:The 4th Matsu Biennial invites artists and creative teams world
 wide to develop new work for the Matsu Islands\, Taiwan\, taking the archi
 pelago itself as its site: its geography\, Cold War history\, marine ecolo
 gy and everyday life.\n\nOrganisation: Matsu Biennial Promotion Committee 
 (Lienchiang County Government and General Association of Chinese Culture)\
 nLocation: Matsu Islands (Nangan\, Beigan\, Dongju\, Xiju)\, Taiwan. Open 
 to individual artists\, creative practitioners and artist teams of any nat
 ionality\, aged 18 and over.\nAward: 4 to 5 proposals are selected\; each 
 in principle receives NTD 800\,000 (approximately USD 25\,000\, tax includ
 ed) in financial support.\nDuration: Selected works must be completed by 1
 0 August 2027\; exhibition planned 20 August to 7 November 2027\n\nMore: h
 ttps://matsubiennial.tw/en/news/details/88?utm_source=artificialnouveaugra
 ntdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://matsubiennial.tw/en/news/details/88?utm_source=artificialnouvea
 ugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Matsu Islands (Nangan\, Beigan\, Dongju\, Xiju)\, Taiwan. Open to 
 individual artists\, creative practitioners and artist teams of any nation
 ality\, aged 18 and over.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:acc-new-york-fellowship-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261104T163759Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261110
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261111
SUMMARY:Deadline: Asian Cultural Council New York Fellowship 2027 (USD 38\,
 000)
DESCRIPTION:The Asian Cultural Council's New York Fellowship brings artists
 \, scholars and arts professionals from Asia to New York City for a six-mo
 nth immersive cultural exchange. SUPPORT: USD 38\,000 for the six-month fe
 llowship.\n\nOrganisation: Asian Cultural Council\nLocation: Six-month fel
 lowship in New York City. For artists\, scholars and arts professionals fr
 om ACC-eligible Asian countries (non-US citizens/residents).\nAward: USD 3
 8\,000 for the six-month fellowship\, covering the immersive cultural exch
 ange in New York City. No application fee.\nDuration: Six months\, in one 
 of two cohorts: January-June 2028 or July-December 2028\n\nMore: https://w
 ww.asianculturalcouncil.org/grant-opportunities?utm_source=artificialnouve
 augrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.asianculturalcouncil.org/grant-opportunities?utm_source=art
 ificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Six-month fellowship in New York City. For artists\, scholars and 
 arts professionals from ACC-eligible Asian countries (non-US citizens/resi
 dents).
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:acc-individual-fellowship-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261104T163759Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261110
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261111
SUMMARY:Deadline: Asian Cultural Council Individual Fellowship 2027 (up to 
 USD 35\,000)
DESCRIPTION:The Asian Cultural Council's Individual Fellowship supports sel
 f-directed exploration and cultural exchange experiences in a new or less 
 familiar environment\, fostering exchange between the United States and As
 ia and within Asia. SUPPORT: up to USD 35\,000 for a 1-to-6-month program 
 (minimum 30 days\; two or more months preferred)\; single or joint applica
 tions with up to 3 participants.\n\nOrganisation: Asian Cultural Council\n
 Location: Self-directed cultural exchange between the US and Asia\, or wit
 hin Asia. For citizens and permanent residents of ACC-eligible countries (
 including the US).\nAward: Up to USD 35\,000 for self-directed exploration
  and cultural exchange of 1 to 6 months. Single or joint applications (up 
 to 3 participants). No application fee.\nDuration: 1 to 6 months (minimum 
 30 days\; 2 or more months preferred)\, with grant activities between 1 Au
 gust 2027 and 31 December 2028\n\nMore: https://www.asianculturalcouncil.o
 rg/grant-opportunities?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=re
 ferral
URL:https://www.asianculturalcouncil.org/grant-opportunities?utm_source=art
 ificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Self-directed cultural exchange between the US and Asia\, or withi
 n Asia. For citizens and permanent residents of ACC-eligible countries (in
 cluding the US).
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:eulsukdo-busan-land-ecological-art-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261104T163759Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261122
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261123
SUMMARY:Deadline: Busan Metropolitan City: Open Call for Land / Ecological 
 Art on Eulsukdo
DESCRIPTION:Busan Metropolitan City invites individuals and teams from arou
 nd the world to propose a site-responsive work of land and ecological art 
 for Eulsukdo\, an estuarine island at the mouth of the Nakdong River\, Sou
 th Korea's longest river.\n\nOrganisation: Busan Metropolitan City\, Urban
  Parks Division\nLocation: Eulsukdo\, Busan\, South Korea (site at 1142-8 
 Hadan-dong\, Saha-gu). Open to individuals and teams worldwide\; the commi
 ssioned work is realised on site.\nAward: One proposal selected. Artwork s
 upport KRW 380\,000\,000 (approx. EUR 235\,000) plus artist fee KRW 20\,00
 0\,000 (approx. EUR 12\,500). No entry fee indicated.\nDuration: Single co
 mmission\; provisional opening May to June 2027.\n\nMore: https://eulsukdo
 -ecoart.com/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://eulsukdo-ecoart.com/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_
 medium=referral
LOCATION:Eulsukdo\, Busan\, South Korea (site at 1142-8 Hadan-dong\, Saha-g
 u). Open to individuals and teams worldwide\; the commissioned work is rea
 lised on site.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:alkazi-curatorial-research-fellowship-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261104T163759Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261107
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261108
SUMMARY:Deadline: Alkazi Foundation: Curatorial Research Fellowship 2027 (w
 ith CWIT and the V&A)
DESCRIPTION:A funded research residency (3rd edition of the Visiting Curato
 rial Research Fellowship) for mid-career cultural producers from India: ar
 tists\, scholars\, writers/editors and curators pursuing humanities-driven
  research in the V&A's global photography and visual-culture collections i
 n London. The awardee is announced in February 2027 and the fellowship sta
 rts April 2027.\n\nOrganisation: Alkazi Foundation for the Arts\, with the
  Charles Wallace India Trust and the Victoria and Albert Museum\nLocation:
  New Delhi\, India (organiser)\; the funded research residency takes place
  at the V&A Photography Section\, London. RESTRICTED: Indian citizens domi
 ciled in India\, aged 25 to 45\, mid-career.\nAward: GBP 1\,600 monthly st
 ipend for 3 to 6 months\, plus a GBP 800 contribution from CWIT towards in
 ternational return airfare\; visa expenses covered by the Alkazi Foundatio
 n. No application fee.\nDuration: 3 to 6 months\n\nMore: https://alkazifou
 ndation.org/call-for-entries-5/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_
 medium=referral
URL:https://alkazifoundation.org/call-for-entries-5/?utm_source=artificialn
 ouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:New Delhi\, India (organiser)\; the funded research residency take
 s place at the V&A Photography Section\, London. RESTRICTED: Indian citize
 ns domiciled in India\, aged 25 to 45\, mid-career.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:yao-residency-02-taiwan-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261104T163759Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261231
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270101
SUMMARY:Deadline: YAO Residency #02 (Taiwan): Research Residency 2027 and E
 xhibition 2028
DESCRIPTION:YAO Residency #02 centres on the translation between culture an
 d material: through living\, research and exchange in Taiwan\, artists eng
 age with different cultural contexts\, local ways of living\, materials an
 d craft practices\, with emphasis on process rather than finished works. O
 NE artist/practitioner is selected for a two-phase program.\n\nOrganisatio
 n: YAO Residency Program (Yao Zuo Zhu Cun Ji Hua)\nLocation: Taiwan. Open 
 worldwide to applicants aged 18 and above\, regardless of nationality\; in
 ternational artists arrange their own entry and visa (YAO can provide an i
 nvitation letter).\nAward: Research Residency 2027: travel support (intern
 ational applicants reimbursed up to NTD 20\,000 for one round-trip to Taiw
 an against receipts)\, production budget up to NTD 20\,000\, living stipen
 d of NTD 10\,000\, accommodation\, Open Studio venue\, local connections\,
  and documentation\, text editing\, translation and promotional support. E
 xhibition Phase 2028: travel support up to NTD 20\,000 again\, a further N
 TD 10\,000 living stipend\, accommodation\, exhibition venue at YAO\, inst
 allation and de-installation assistance\, and exhibition documentation. Ap
 plication fee: NTD 300 for Taiwan-based applicants (bank transfer) or USD 
 10 for international applicants (PayPal)\, non-refundable.\nDuration: Two 
 phases: research residency 21 August to 21 November 2027 with Open Studio 
 27 October to 16 November 2027\, then a formal exhibition at YAO in 2028 (
 expected to run at least six weeks\, dates agreed with the artist). The se
 lected artist commits to both phases.\n\nMore: https://docs.google.com/for
 ms/d/e/1FAIpQLSfQ5-RBrfPckf4O9A5LeDrAzbFlXHzBkYrpPyTiy3HeKc8BkQ/viewform?u
 tm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSfQ5-RBrfPckf4O9A5LeDrAzbFlXHz
 BkYrpPyTiy3HeKc8BkQ/viewform?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_med
 ium=referral
LOCATION:Taiwan. Open worldwide to applicants aged 18 and above\, regardles
 s of nationality\; international artists arrange their own entry and visa 
 (YAO can provide an invitation letter).
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:tarbell-fellowship-2027-28@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261104T163759Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261122
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261123
SUMMARY:Deadline: Tarbell Fellowship 2027-28 (AI journalism)
DESCRIPTION:A year-long fellowship for journalists covering artificial inte
 lligence. Fellows complete a three-month full-time remote programme on AI 
 and journalism fundamentals\, attend a weeklong summit\, then work for nin
 e months as reporters embedded in a partner newsroom (current partners are
  in Hong Kong\, London\, Los Angeles\, New York\, San Francisco\, Seattle\
 , Washington DC and Cambridge).\n\nOrganisation: Tarbell Center for AI Jou
 rnalism\nLocation: Remote training\, then newsroom placement in the US\, U
 K or Hong Kong. In person.\nAward: USD 75\,000 to 120\,000 depending on ex
 perience and placement cost of living\; senior fellows (7+ years experienc
 e) USD 115\,000 to 135\,000. Summit travel and accommodation covered. No a
 pplication fee.\nDuration: 12 months: remote training 7 June to 6 August 2
 027\, in-person summit August 2027\, newsroom placement September 2027 to 
 May 2028 (extendable by one year).\n\nMore: https://www.tarbellcenter.org/
 fellowship?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.tarbellcenter.org/fellowship?utm_source=artificialnouveaugr
 antdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Remote training\, then newsroom placement in the US\, UK or Hong K
 ong. In person.
END:VEVENT
